 `omni_manifold` | present |\n| 46 | `ptr_from_parts` | present |\n\nThe C library's undefined dynamic symbols are only toolchain/libc/libm\ndependencies: `_ITM_deregisterTMCloneTable`, `_ITM_registerTMCloneTable`,\n`__cxa_finalize`, `__gmon_start__`, `malloc`, and `sqrtf`.\n# Error Surface\n\nThe C source has no `assert`, `RETURN_ERROR`, error enum, `return -1`, or\nexplicit `return NULL`. It reports geometric rejection by leaving\n`c2Manifold.count` at zero, and reports unsupported type dispatch by doing\nnothing. These are all defined rejection branches found in the source.\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result |\n|---|----------|----------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| E01 | `c2MakeProxy` | `type` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or any value outside the three handled switch cases | output proxy remains byte-for-byte unchanged |\n| E02 | `c2CircletoCircleManifold` | `dot(B.p-A.p, B.p-A.p) >= (A.r+B.r)^2` | `m->count = 0`; remaining manifold bytes unchanged |\n| E03 | `c2CircletoAABBManifold` | squared distance from circle center to clamped AABB point is `>= A.r^2` | `m->count = 0`; remaining manifold bytes unchanged |\n| E04 | `c2CircletoCapsuleManifold` | GJK distance is `>= A.r+B.r` | `m->count = 0`; remaining manifold bytes unchanged |\n| E05 | `c2AABBtoAABBManifold` | x overlap `dx < 0` | `m->count = 0`; immediate return |\n| E06 | `c2AABBtoAABBManifold` | x overlap is nonnegative and y overlap `dy < 0` | `m->count = 0`; immediate return |\n| E07 | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | `d < 1e-6`, reference-face path selected, and first/second side-plane clipping yields fewer than two points | immediate return with the manifold state produced so far |\n| E08 | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | `d < 1e-6`, first capsule-face path selected, and side-plane clipping yields fewer than two points | immediate return with the manifold state produced so far |\n| E09 | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | `d < 1e-6`, second capsule-face path selected, and side-plane clipping yields fewer than two points | immediate return with the manifold state produced so far |\n| E10 | `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` | GJK distance `d >= A.r` | `m->count = 0`; no contact |\n| E11 | `c2CapsuletoCapsuleManifold` | GJK distance is `>= A.r+B.r` | `m->count = 0`; remaining manifold bytes unchanged |\n| E12 | `c2Collide` | valid outer `typeA`, but `typeB` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or an out-of-range integer | `m->count = 0`; no inner switch case runs |\n| E13 | `c2Collide` | `typeA` is `C2_TYPE_POLY` or an out-of-range integer | `m->count = 0`; no outer switch case runs |\n| E14 | `omni_manifold` | either dispatch type has no `c2Collide` case (`C2_TYPE_POLY` or out-of-range), while execution reaches `c2Collide` | `m->count = 0` |\n\n## FFI Boundary Limits\n\nThe public C functions do not validate null pointers, zero counts, oversized\ncounts, invalid polygon counts, or out-of-range indices. Passing those values\nto a path that dereferences/indexes them has undefined behavior, so C defines\nno error code or sentinel to compare. Differential tests cover null optional\npointers where the C source explicitly checks them (`c2GJK` transforms,\noutputs, iterations, and cache; `c2CapsuletoPolyManifold` transform), zero\niteration counts where no dereference occurs (`c2Norms`), and invalid enums on\nthe defined no-dispatch paths above. `ptr_from_parts` itself falls off the end\nfor unsupported enum values, which is also undefined behavior rather than a\ndefined rejection.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
